# Fuzz corpora and crash payloads are raw byte streams; the bytes ARE the
# input, so text normalization (CRLF handling) must never touch them. The
# committed seeds join the two ephemeral dirs: several carry a bare CR or a
# trailing space as part of the reproduction (`&"X-\r:`, `!y5%7c `), which a
# contributor with core.autocrlf enabled would otherwise silently rewrite.
fuzz/corpus/** -text
fuzz/artifacts/** -text
fuzz/seeds/** -text
